Double-shelled zinc-cobalt sulfide rhombic dodecahedral cages are synthesized by a sequential chemical etching and sulfurization strategy. With the structural advantages, the well-defined doubleshelled zinc-cobalt sulfide cages exhibit much enhanced electrochemical performance compared to the single-shelled counterpart as electrode materials for hybrid supercapacitors.
